// ProjectDeliveryS680 — Sprint 680: The authoring family joins keel record. Under D0451 (d0399 option A, the human's word 2026-09-11) the nine authoring verbs - add-task, new sprint, append-result, append-gate-result, apply-review, record-measurement, snapshot-indicators, reverify, mint - leave the top-level dispatch and become sub-verbs of `keel record`, each named for the fact it writes (task, sprint, result, gate-result, review, measurement, indicator-snapshot, reverify, mint) and each keeping its flags, in the sprint 512 shape (D0273): a committed transform rewrites every call site in the same commit, no alias window, and the pre-fold binary is held equal to the post-fold binary on every moved verb with the written tree compared too, since a writer's output is the file it changes. Delivers the third of the five folds dcRemainingCliFamilies names; the dispatch count hardening reads drops 58 to 49. CHANGE.. EXECUTE. 3 pts.
