    verification authoringFamilyFoldRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "44963881-74da-470b-91ba-a64a309d5437"; :>> title = "Sprint 680 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-12"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN: one, recorded. FINDING: the touched suite went red once on the VERIFIER run (780 passed, 1 failed): control_structure_is_computed.rs:74 asserted the computed action cmdAddTask, a name derived from a folded verb that the transform rule (keel <verb>) cannot see, and the primary had passed only the unit tests naming it (whose fixtures are synthetic). Fixed to cmdRecord, 3 passed. No new item (D0131): the D0425 split caught it before any result was recorded, which is the control working, and issue497 renames every one of these actions next, so a name-bound check written now would be rewritten with them. FINDING: a control bound to a verb's spelling does not follow the verb when it moves - the pre-bash human-judgment check (K7) read one token after keel, so apply-review's Ask would have gone silent at `record review` with every test still green, because no test asked the two-token question. Fixed at the root in this sprint: the check reads verb and verb+sub-verb and bash_classify holds one positive and one negative; no new item (D0131) - the control is in d0451's own commit and the D0452/D0453 folds inherit the two-token check. FINDING: the fold makes the STPA control structure read better by disappearance - seven never-analysed write actions collapsed into cmdRecord, 49/39 to 41/32 open under stpa-currency, and 8 UCA contexts name cmdAppendResult, an action no longer computed. Recorded as issue497, resolved by dcRecordSubVerbsAreControlActions (one computed action per sub-verb of a routing write command; then a stpa-self run over them), which the D0452 and D0453 folds need before they land or the same collapse recurs for gate, audit and github. FINDING: the 679 retro's carried item is closed here - `record`'s sub-verb inventory is now held equal to its router by the_record_sub_verbs_match_the_fact, beside the_lens_inventory_matches_the_router that already held cmd_show to LENS_NAMES; no new item (D0131)."; }
